Subject: [PATCH] agent: keep the radios in an empty station snapshot

analyze_sta_list copies the agent's radios into the command's model but
not their count; the OneWifi translator sets the count only while it
walks associated clients. A full associated-clients snapshot with no
client left the model without radios, so every reporting RUID was
unknown and orchestration rejected the snapshot ("Rejecting STA snapshot
with missing, invalid, or unknown reporting RUID").

Such a snapshot is exactly the withdrawal of an AP's last client. The
agent kept that client and reported it again in its Topology Responses
until the station aged out (about 3 minutes); once the client left its
new AP, the controller took the stale report as its association (the
wired extender at the edge of the RDK lab rooms, which usually serves
one client: home-a-flash-crowd failed in every suite run). Copy the
count with the radios.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/agent/dm_easy_mesh_agent.cpp
+++ b/src/agent/dm_easy_mesh_agent.cpp
@@ -150,6 +150,11 @@
     for (unsigned int i = 0; i < m_num_radios; i++) {
         dm.m_radio[i] = m_radio[i];
     }
+    /* The translator sets the radio count only while it walks associated
+     * clients: a full snapshot with none left the command's model without
+     * radios, every reporting RUID unknown, and the snapshot (the withdrawal
+     * of the AP's last client) rejected. */
+    dm.set_num_radios(m_num_radios);
 
     dm.m_num_bss = m_num_bss;
     for (unsigned int i = 0; i < EM_MAX_BSSS; i++) {
